{
  "workflowId": "300000330254751",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_RECEIPT_ACCOUNTING_ACCRUAL_CLEARING_ANALYST",
  "name": "Receipt Accounting Accrual Clearing Analyst",
  "description": "This AI agent analyzes receipt accounting manual accrual clearing transactions and generates a summarized view of cleared accrual balances.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769073416582"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is Open Accrual Flow"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1769073657558",
            "false": "1769073736639"
          },
          "code": "IS_OPEN_ACCRUAL_FLOW",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1769073416582",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769073416583_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.FlowType === 'OPEN'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Clear Open Accrual Balance"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CLEAR_OPEN_ACCRUAL_BALANCE",
          "id": "1769073657558",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769073657560_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\nOpen Accrual Balance: ```{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OpenAccrualBalance}}```.  This is the amount remaining on the account.\n\nReason: ```{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Reason}}```.  These are keywords provided by the user to clear the accrual. \n\nAge: ```{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Age}}```. The number of days since the last activity on the purchase order.\n\nCurrency: ```{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Currency}}```.  The currency of the remaining balance.\n\n\n### Task\nAssume the role of an accountant who is skilled at generating auditable reasons for clearing off the open accrual balance in the application.\n\nGenerate a sentence containing that details why the accrual balance is being cleared.\n\nUse only the Context section above.\n\nDo not add any additional interpretations and accounting policy statements. \n\nDo not generate any reason not directly included in the context section above. Use only the information available to you. \n\n\n### Output Format\n\n\"The open accrual balance is cleared because <insert reason>.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Accrual Clearing Summaries"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ACCRUAL_CLEARING_SUMMARIES",
          "id": "1769073736639",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769073736641_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your entire knowledge is limited ONLY to information contained in this prompt. Do not include any information for demo or sample purposes that is not referenced in the variables below. Only include one output, do not suggest any alternatives.\n\n## Context\nAssume the role of a proficient and professional accountant. \n\nYou excel at reviewing write-offs, and summarizing the clearing data.\n\n\n## Task\nCategorize the reasons for write-offs into general, high level groups. Explain these groups\n\nExtract the top couple suppliers. List them their main reasons and their categories. Do not include amounts or counts.\n\nExtract and highlight any anomalies or unusual entries that may require further investigation. Specifically look for any amounts higher than usual. In addition also look for records where reason for write off are missing or not properly documented. For such records, provide PO number, supplier, amount and reason.\n\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nSummary must be presented in three bolded sections using a numbered bulleted list. \n\nDo not perform any calculations, summations, or count aggregations.\n\nDo not display counts.\n\nDo not refer to any additional information in the response except what is provide in the input data.\n\nRestrict summary to 300 words.\n\nConclude with the following statement \"\"This summary provides a snapshot of the dataset, helping to identify patterns, potential issues, and areas requiring further analysis. It's important to note that this is a partial view, and further investigation could reveal additional insights.\"\"\n\nDo not provide any other recommendations.\n\n\n## Manual Clearing Data\n The dataset contains purchase order records detailing various write-off transactions.\n\n``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ManualClearingData}} ```\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
      "errorHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "EMAIL",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "name": "toList",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "ccList",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
